commit 37f50e75e02378045a8958afd960601903615d3e

C03: a proper name that no catalog claims is read once as an application presence so the reply can name it (APPS1549)

APPS1535 measured that «Y quema, abre Saint Rose.» (H0249), with the spoken opener stripped, fell into the generic out-of-catalog answer («No puedo hacer eso, está fuera de mi ámbito.») that never names Saint Rose, and that its variants ended with the model asking whether to open a name that exists nowhere. A capitalized bare name (every word capitalized, no article, at most four words) after a plain open verb (abre/abrí/open), claimed by no application or game catalog entry, no near catalog name and no public site, is now read once as an application presence (app.installed); the verified absence lets the reply say it does not find that application, naming it. Registry-wide recogniser diff with the real Start catalog: only H0249 changes (None → app.installed). The constraint acknowledgement prompt now says the acknowledgement is the whole reply (no question or offer of help): SYSTEM1547 measured «No uses Python.» losing its final to a trailing help question and an empty retry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


